{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"f6e3c1bb-ed83-41d6-b20c-fbbdfa565f83","title":"Ray diagram for a converging lens"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f6e3c1bb-ed83-41d6-b20c-fbbdfa565f83","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A converging lens brings parallel rays toward a focus. Place an upright object at twice the focal length on the left.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Converging lens: ray diagram"},{"op":"figure","id":"lens_diagram","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-5,5],"y":[-3,3],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"axis","from":[-4.8,0],"to":[4.8,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"polyline","points":[[0,-2.6],[-0.3,-1.8],[-0.4,0],[-0.3,1.8],[0,2.6],[0.3,1.8],[0.4,0],[0.3,-1.8],[0,-2.6]],"closed":true,"smooth":true},{"kind":"point","id":"center","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"point","id":"focus_left","at":[-2,0],"label":"F"},{"kind":"point","id":"focus_right","at":[2,0],"label":"F"},{"kind":"point","id":"object_top","at":[-4,2]},{"kind":"segment","id":"object","from":[-4,0],"to":{"at":"object_top"},"arrow":true,"label":"object"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"distance","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"d_o=2f"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f6e3c1bb-ed83-41d6-b20c-fbbdfa565f83","step":{"id":"s2","script":"From the object's tip, draw a ray parallel to the axis. After the lens, it passes through the far focus.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"parallel_ray","on":"lens_diagram","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"lens_hit","at":[0,2]},{"kind":"segment","id":"incoming","from":{"at":"object_top"},"to":{"at":"lens_hit"},"arrow":true},{"kind":"segment","id":"refracted","from":{"at":"lens_hit"},"to":[4,-2],"arrow":true}]},{"op":"text","id":"rule_one","anchor":{"el":"distance","side":"below","gap":0.1},"content":"Parallel ray → far focus"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f6e3c1bb-ed83-41d6-b20c-fbbdfa565f83","step":{"id":"s3","script":"A second ray travels straight through the lens center. Where the two rays meet locates the image tip.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"central_ray","on":"lens_diagram","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"through_center","from":{"at":"object_top"},"to":{"on":"refracted","t":1},"arrow":true},{"kind":"point","id":"image_tip","at":{"hit":["refracted","through_center"]}}]},{"op":"text","id":"rule_two","anchor":{"el":"rule_one","side":"below","gap":0.1},"content":"Central ray → straight through"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"The rays meet below the axis. Is the image upright or inverted?","expected_gist":"Inverted: the object's tip is above the axis, but its image is below."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"f6e3c1bb-ed83-41d6-b20c-fbbdfa565f83","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Draw the image from the axis to the intersection. It is real, inverted, and the same size, at twice the focal length.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"image_result","on":"lens_diagram","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"image_arrow","from":[4,0],"to":{"at":"image_tip"},"arrow":true,"label":"image"},{"kind":"measure","from":[0,-2.65],"to":[4,-2.65],"label":"2f"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"rule_two","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"d_i=2f,\\qquad m=-\\frac{d_i}{d_o}=-1"},{"op":"text","id":"summary","anchor":{"el":"result","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Real • inverted • same size"}],"checkpoint":null}}
